{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is a lawful "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so every generic algorithm runs on it, including those that need"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge storage."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches instead: Traversal’s "},{"code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and ShortestPaths’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" states over a finite set, number them and use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A grid is numbered row-major."}]},{"text":"The closure","anchor":"The-closure","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"successors(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", once per edge, as any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sequence<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", such as an array or a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list. A specialized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once. "},{"code":"successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"outDegree(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call it once each, and "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" once per vertex."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex. This is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not checked, and a closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm. Each target is checked to be a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and yields","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them by count. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy.filter"},{"text":" calls its predicate per element and carries the unfiltered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterator’s state, which costs more per edge.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Positions","anchor":"Positions","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge’s position is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":", which holds its source, its rank in the source’s row, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(source, rank)"},{"type":"text","text":", which is unique even among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges and self-loops. Because the position carries the target, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and a weight closure reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.target"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge indices."}]},{"text":"Attached values","anchor":"Attached-values","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph"},{"text":", because ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(source, rank)"},{"text":" has a dense offset only after every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"earlier row is counted. Keep vertex values in an array of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexCount"},{"text":" indexed by vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compute edge values from the position (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.source"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.target"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is not "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because a closure has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity and is not "},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L48","fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"